# ============================================================================
# Gimboot — static-asset redirect fallback
#
# PRODUCTION IS A WORKER, NOT PAGES.
# `wrangler.toml` sets `run_worker_first = ["/*"]`, so every production
# request is handled by `src/index.js` first. The Worker performs the real
# canonical redirects:
#
#   /index.html, /index.htm       -> 301 /            (query dropped)
#   /game.html?id=<valid>        -> 301 /play/{id}/{slug}  (one hop)
#   /game.html (no id)           -> 301 /
#   /game?id=<valid>             -> 301 /play/{id}/{slug}  (one hop)
#   /game (no/invalid id)        -> 404
#
# This file is only a fallback for a pure static deployment (plain asset
# hosting), where no server-side catalog lookup exists. See the note below for
# why the legacy game paths are deliberately not listed here.
# ============================================================================

# 1. Duplicate root documents -> canonical root
/index.html / 301
/index.htm / 301

# NOTE: no /game or /game.html rules here. Production is Worker-first
# (`run_worker_first = ["/*"]`), so src/index.js owns those paths and can do a
# server-side catalog lookup. The asset binding also applies this file to
# env.ASSETS.fetch(), so a redirect rule here would make the canonical /play
# renderer unable to read game.html and return 503. A pure static deployment
# simply serves game.html (marked noindex) instead of redirecting it.
